## 1. Executive Summary & System Overview

### 1.1 What is NeuroNest Kids?

**NeuroNest Kids** is an AI-powered, child-centric educational web application built from the ground up for children with **autism spectrum disorder (ASD)**, learning disabilities, and developmental differences. The platform provides a safe, calm, and highly adaptive digital learning environment that adjusts itself in real time to each child's unique cognitive pace, sensory preferences, and emotional state.

The application is designed around the core insight that children with ASD often respond best to structured, predictable interactions with clear visual feedback, consistent routines, and just-right challenges — not too hard (causing frustration) and not too easy (causing boredom). NeuroNest Kids uses an embedded AI engine to continuously monitor performance and automatically calibrate difficulty, pacing, and emotional support.

### 1.2 Mission Statement

> *"Learning should meet every child where they are — not where the curriculum expects them to be."*

NeuroNest Kids ensures that every game session is personalised and encouraging. When a child struggles, the AI detects it within 2–3 answers and immediately simplifies the challenge. When a child excels, the AI progressively introduces complexity — all without the child ever feeling tested.

### 1.3 Who Uses It?

| User Type | Role | Primary Actions |
|---|---|---|
| **Parent / Caregiver** | Account owner | Create child profiles, review reports, set limits, configure AI |
| **Child** | Learner | Play games, earn stars, learn through play |
| **Educator (future)** | Supervisor | Monitor class-wide progress, assign learning goals |

### 1.4 System Context

NeuroNest Kids is a **Single-Page Application (SPA)** served over the web, backed by a fully managed cloud infrastructure:

- The **frontend** is a React application bundled by Vite, deployed as static files.
- The **backend** is entirely powered by **Supabase** — a Firebase-alternative built on PostgreSQL — that handles authentication, row-level-security data access, real-time subscriptions, and edge functions.
- An **AI orchestration layer** runs as a Supabase Edge Function (`adaptive-ai-helper`) that receives gameplay telemetry and returns personalised encouragement, hints, and difficulty recommendations.

### 1.5 Design Philosophy

- **Neurodiversity-first**: Minimal clutter, predictable layouts, calming color palette (pastels + purples), and optional reduced animations.
- **Emoji-forward**: Every concept is paired with an emoji or cartoon for children who struggle with text.
- **Voice-paired**: All questions and feedback are simultaneously spoken via the Web Speech API.
- **Parent visibility**: A full reporting dashboard with PIN-gate gives parents deep insight without interrupting the child's session.
- **Data sovereignty**: All data stays within the parent's account; no data is shared or sold.

### 1.6 Key Metrics & Scope

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Total interactive games | 20 |
| Questions per game session | 10 |
| Difficulty levels | 5 (dynamically adjusted by AI) |
| Database tables | 7 |
| Custom React hooks | 12 |
| React components | 32 (+ 49 UI primitives) |
| Supporting UI pages | 7 |
| Supabase edge functions | 1 (adaptive-ai-helper) |

