## 3. Features — Child & Parent

### 3.1 Child-Facing Features

#### 🎮 Adaptive Game Library
The platform provides 20 educational mini-games covering five learning domains:
- **Literacy**: Alphabet, Vowels, Consonants, Letter Tracing
- **Numeracy**: Numbers, Counting, Comparing, Clock
- **World Knowledge**: Animals, Body Parts, Kitchen, Home Tools, Fruits, Weather
- **Cognitive**: Memory, Emotions, Drag-Drop Sorting, Music, Color Recognition, Shape Matching

Each game consists of **10 rounds** with immediate audio-visual feedback. All games share the same scoring system (+10 per correct answer) and star rating (1–3 stars based on accuracy ≥50%, ≥70%, ≥90%).

#### 🤖 Real-Time AI Difficulty Adaptation
The AI continuously monitors five signals:
1. **Consecutive wrong answers** — triggers immediate difficulty drop
2. **Consecutive correct answers (streak)** — triggers difficulty increase
3. **Overall session accuracy** — influences long-term base level
4. **Response time** — fast responses suggest confidence
5. **Session duration** — fatigue detection triggers break suggestions

Based on these signals the AI moves the child through 5 tiers without disrupting gameplay:

| Level | Name | What Changes in AlphabetGame |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Very Easy | Word + Emoji shown; far-apart letter options (A, H, P, Z) |
| 2 | Easy | Word + Emoji shown; slightly spread options |
| 3 | Normal | Default behaviour; random options |
| 4 | Hard | Word shown; similar/confusing letters as options (B, D, P, Q) |
| 5 | Expert | **Emoji only** — word hidden; confusing letter options |

#### 🔊 Voice & Sound Feedback
Every game question is spoken aloud using the **Web Speech API**. Sound effects are generated in real-time via the **Web Audio API** — no file downloads needed. Parents can disable sounds in settings.

#### 🌟 Rewards & Star System
Each game session is rated 1–3 stars based on final accuracy. Stars are displayed on the game-complete screen with a satisfying spin animation. A persistent streak counter rewards consecutive correct answers.

#### 🦮 Animated Guide Mascot
Every game screen has an animated **GuideMascot** that:
- Shows contextual encouragement messages in a speech bubble
- Switches between `happy`, `thinking`, `celebrating`, and `sad` emotions
- Uses a typewriter effect for text display
- Is present even when the AI overlay is visible

#### 🎙️ Voice Input
A `VoiceButton` component integrates with the Web Speech API allowing children to speak their answers (where supported by the browser).

### 3.2 Parent-Facing Features

#### 🔐 PIN-Protected Dashboard
The parent dashboard is accessible after authentication. Sensitive sections (Reports, Settings) are additionally protected by a **4-digit PIN** stored locally. First-time parents set a PIN; returning parents must enter it to access protected areas.

#### 📊 Progress Analytics & Reports
The `ParentReportDashboard` provides:
- **Accuracy trends** across all games and time periods
- **Game-by-game breakdown** — best game, worst game, average accuracy
- **Mistake analysis** — which specific questions were most commonly wrong
- **Session timeline** — visual history of past game sessions
- **Strength/challenge identification** — categories the child excels in vs. needs practice

#### 📡 Real-Time Remote Control
Via the `ParentRemoteControl` component, parents can:
- Set the child's **maximum games per session**
- Set a **daily time limit** in minutes
- Toggle **difficulty auto-adjustment** on/off
- Enable/disable specific **game categories**
- Set a **manual difficulty level override** (1–5)
- Enable **focus mode** (hides distracting elements)
- Configure **break reminders** (interval in minutes)
- Set **age filter** for content appropriateness

All remote control settings are stored in the `remote_control_settings` table with realtime sync, meaning changes take effect in the child's active session within seconds.

#### 🔔 Automated Parent Alerts
The `useParentAlerts` hook sends the parent a notification when:
- A child achieves a **milestone** (e.g., 90%+ accuracy, long streak)
- A child is **struggling** (3+ consecutive wrong answers, low accuracy)

These alerts appear in the `ParentAlertCenter` component and are logged in the database.

#### 📅 Daily Schedule Builder
Parents can build a **structured daily schedule** using the `DailyScheduleBuilder` component — specifying which learning categories are played at which times of day, supporting children who thrive on routine.

#### ♿ Accessibility Settings
The `ParentAccessibilitySettings` and `SensorySettingsPanel` components allow parents to configure:
- Font size (Standard / Large / Extra Large)
- Color theme (Default / High Contrast / Soft Pastels)
- Reduce animations toggle
- Text-to-speech speed and voice selection
- Button tap size enlargement

---

## 4. Games Catalogue — All 20 Games

Each game follows the same structural pattern: 10 rounds, immediate feedback, stars on completion, and data saved to `game_sessions`.

### 4.1 Literacy Games

#### 🔤 Alphabet Game (`/games/alphabet/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Identify the starting letter of a word.
**Mechanic**: An emoji and/or word is shown; the child picks the correct starting letter from a 2×2 grid of options.
**AI Adaptation**: Options change from far-apart letters (Easy) → similar/confusing letters (Hard); word label hides at Expert level (emoji only).
**Options**: 4 letter choices | **Alphabet Pool**: All 26 letters (A–Z)

#### 🔵 Vowels Game (`/games/vowels/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Identify vowels (A, E, I, O, U) vs consonants.
**Mechanic**: A letter is shown; the child chooses "Vowel" or "Consonant".
**AI Adaptation**: Confusing borderline letters introduced at higher difficulty.

#### 🔴 Consonants Game (`/games/consonants/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Recognize consonants and their sounds.
**Mechanic**: A word/image is shown; the child identifies the first consonant sound.

#### ✏️ Letter Tracing Game (`/games/letters/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Develop fine motor skills through letter tracing.
**Mechanic**: An SVG canvas is displayed; the child traces a letter by dragging their finger/mouse along the guide path.

### 4.2 Numeracy Games

#### 🔢 Numbers Game (`/games/numbers/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Recognise single and double-digit numbers.
**Mechanic**: A numeral is displayed (with optional voice reading); the child picks the matching word ("Seven", "12", etc.) from 4 options.

#### 🧮 Count Along Game (`/games/counting/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Count objects accurately.
**Mechanic**: A group of emojis is shown (1–10 items); the child selects the correct count from 4 answer buttons.

#### ⚖️ Compare Items Game (`/games/comparing/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Understand "more than", "less than", and "equal".
**Mechanic**: Two groups of objects are shown; the child selects the comparison operator.

#### 🕐 Clock Game (`/games/clock/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Tell the time from an analogue clock.
**Mechanic**: An SVG analogue clock face is shown; the child selects the correct time (e.g., "3:30") from 4 options.

### 4.3 World Knowledge Games

#### 🦁 Animals Game (`/games/animals/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Identify animals by name and sound.
**Mechanic**: An animal emoji is shown; the child selects the correct name. Sound cues play the animal's sound.

#### 🫀 Body Parts Game (`/games/bodyparts/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Learn body part names.
**Mechanic**: A body part is highlighted on an illustrated body diagram; the child names it.

#### 🍴 Kitchen Game (`/games/kitchen/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Recognise kitchen items and their uses.
**Mechanic**: An object emoji is shown; the child identifies it by name or use.

#### 🔧 Home Tools Game (`/games/hometools/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Recognise household tools and items.
**Mechanic**: Similar to Kitchen game — emoji + 4-option multiple choice.

#### 🍎 Fruits Learning Game (`/games/fruits/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Identify fruits and vegetables.
**Mechanic**: A food emoji is displayed with the category label; the child selects the name.
**Items**: Apple, Banana, Orange, Strawberry, Grapes, Watermelon, Mango, Pineapple, Cherry, Peach, Carrot, Broccoli, Tomato, Cucumber, Corn, Potato.

#### 🌦️ Weather Game (`/games/weather/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Identify weather conditions.
**Mechanic**: A weather emoji/animation is shown; the child names the condition (Sunny, Rainy, Cloudy, Snowy, etc.)

### 4.4 Cognitive Games

#### 🧠 Memory Game (`/games/memory/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Develop short-term visual memory.
**Mechanic**: A grid of face-down cards is shown; the child flips pairs to find matching emojis. Fewer pairs = easier; full 6×6 grid = expert.

#### 😊 Emotions Game (`/games/emotions/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Recognise and name emotions — critical for children with ASD.
**Mechanic**: A cartoon face/emoji showing an emotion is displayed; the child selects the emotion name ("Happy", "Sad", "Angry", "Surprised", etc.).

#### 📦 Drag & Drop Sorting Game (`/games/sorting/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Categorise items logically.
**Mechanic**: Items appear on screen and must be dragged into the correct category zone (Fruits / Animals / Vehicles / etc.).

#### 🎵 Music Game (`/games/music/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Recognise musical instruments.
**Mechanic**: An instrument emoji or image is shown (with optional sound); the child names the instrument.

#### 🎨 Color Recognition Game (`/games/colors/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Name colors.
**Mechanic**: A colored square/panel is shown; the child selects the correct color name.
**Colors**: Red, Blue, Yellow, Green, Orange, Purple, Pink, Brown, Black, White, Gray, Cyan.

#### 🔷 Shape Matching Game (`/games/shapes/:childId`)
**Learning Goal**: Identify 2D geometric shapes.
**Mechanic**: A shape is shown; the child names it.
**Shapes**: Circle, Square, Triangle, Rectangle, Star, Heart, Diamond, Oval, Pentagon, Hexagon.

