## 6. Entity-Relationship (ER) Diagram

The following Mermaid ERD shows all tables and their relationships.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    AUTH_USERS {
        uuid id PK
        text email
        timestamp created_at
    }

    PROFILES {
        uuid id PK
        uuid user_id FK
        text email
        text display_name
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp updated_at
    }

    USER_ROLES {
        uuid id PK
        uuid user_id FK
        enum role
    }

    PARENTAL_SETTINGS {
        uuid id PK
        uuid parent_id FK
        int session_duration_minutes
        bool sound_enabled
        bool animations_enabled
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp updated_at
    }

    CHILD_PROFILES {
        uuid id PK
        uuid parent_id FK
        text name
        int age
        text avatar
        timestamp created_at
        timestamp updated_at
    }

    GAME_SESSIONS {
        uuid id PK
        uuid child_id FK
        text game_type
        int score
        int total_questions
        int correct_answers
        int wrong_answers
        jsonb mistakes
        int max_streak
        int duration_seconds
        timestamp created_at
    }

    CHILD_BEHAVIOR_PROFILES {
        uuid id PK
        uuid child_id FK
        varchar preferred_pace
        int attention_span_minutes
        varchar best_time_of_day
        bool prefers_sounds
        bool prefers_animations
        decimal average_accuracy
        int frustration_threshold
        jsonb strong_categories
        jsonb challenging_categories
        int current_difficulty_level
        jsonb recommended_games
        jsonb ai_insights
        timestamp last_ai_analysis
    }

    REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTINGS {
        uuid id PK
        uuid child_id FK
        uuid parent_id FK
        int difficulty_level
        bool auto_adjust_difficulty
        jsonb enabled_categories
        int daily_time_limit
        bool focus_mode
        bool break_reminders
        int break_interval_minutes
        int max_games_per_session
        jsonb schedule
        timestamp updated_at
    }

    AUTH_USERS ||--o| PROFILES : "has"
    AUTH_USERS ||--o{ USER_ROLES : "assigned"
    AUTH_USERS ||--o| PARENTAL_SETTINGS : "configures"
    AUTH_USERS ||--o{ CHILD_PROFILES : "manages"
    CHILD_PROFILES ||--o{ GAME_SESSIONS : "plays"
    CHILD_PROFILES ||--o| CHILD_BEHAVIOR_PROFILES : "has AI profile"
    CHILD_PROFILES ||--o| REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTINGS : "controlled by"
    AUTH_USERS ||--o{ REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTINGS : "parent controls"
```

### 6.1 ER Relationship Descriptions

| Relationship | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `AUTH_USERS` → `PROFILES` | 1-to-1 | Created by trigger on signup |
| `AUTH_USERS` → `USER_ROLES` | 1-to-many | Currently only 'parent' role used |
| `AUTH_USERS` → `PARENTAL_SETTINGS` | 1-to-1 | Created by trigger on signup |
| `AUTH_USERS` → `CHILD_PROFILES` | 1-to-many | A parent can have multiple children |
| `CHILD_PROFILES` → `GAME_SESSIONS` | 1-to-many | Each game play = one session record |
| `CHILD_PROFILES` → `CHILD_BEHAVIOR_PROFILES` | 1-to-1 | One AI profile per child |
| `CHILD_PROFILES` → `REMOTE_CONTROL_SETTINGS` | 1-to-1 | One remote config per child |

