## 9. Authentication & Security

### 9.1 Authentication Flow

```
User visits NeuroNest Kids
         │
         ▼
    Landing Page
         │
    "Get Started"
         │
         ▼
    Auth.tsx (Login or Sign Up)
         │
    ┌────┴────┐
    │         │
  Sign Up   Sign In
    │         │
    ▼         ▼
  Supabase Auth (email + password)
    │
    ├── On sign up: trigger fires automatically
    │   ├── Creates record in profiles
    │   ├── Creates record in user_roles (role='parent')
    │   └── Creates record in parental_settings
    │
    ▼
  JWT issued → stored in browser (Supabase SDK handles refresh)
    │
    ▼
  Redirect to ParentDashboard
```

### 9.2 Row-Level Security (RLS)

Every database table has RLS enabled. Even if a user obtains a valid JWT, they can only access rows that belong to them:

| Table | Policy Rule |
|---|---|
| `profiles` | `auth.uid() = user_id` |
| `user_roles` | `auth.uid() = user_id` |
| `child_profiles` | `auth.uid() = parent_id` |
| `parental_settings` | `auth.uid() = parent_id` |
| `game_sessions` | Parent owns the child via `child_profiles` |
| `child_behavior_profiles` | Parent owns the child via `child_profiles` |
| `remote_control_settings` | Parent owns the child via `child_profiles` |

This means: **a parent can never see another parent's children's data, even if they have an authenticated session.**

### 9.3 Parent PIN System

The parent dashboard provides an additional local security layer:

```
Parent tries to access: View Reports OR Settings
              │
              ▼
    ParentPinGate.tsx
              │
    ┌─────────┴──────────┐
    │                    │
  PIN set?           PIN not set?
    │                    │
    ▼                    ▼
  Enter PIN          Create new 4-digit PIN
    │                    │
    ▼                    ▼
  Verify against      Store in localStorage
  localStorage
    │
    ▼
  Access granted (session-valid, no timer)
```

> **Note**: The PIN lives in `localStorage`. For production deployment, consider encrypting it or using `sessionStorage` for automatic expiry on tab close.

### 9.4 Data Privacy

- All data is stored in the Supabase project's PostgreSQL instance.
- No analytics, advertising, or third-party tracking is implemented.
- Game session data is structured (never includes biometric data).
- Parents can delete child profiles, which cascades to delete all associated sessions and behavioral profiles.

### 9.5 Edge Function Security

The `adaptive-ai-helper` edge function is invoked via `supabase.functions.invoke()`, which automatically attaches the user's JWT. The function verifies the JWT before processing any request. No unauthenticated calls can reach the AI layer.

