## 11. Deployment & Environment Setup

### 11.1 Prerequisites

| Requirement | Version | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Node.js | ≥ 18.x | LTS recommended |
| Bun | ≥ 1.x | Used as the package manager |
| Git | ≥ 2.x | Version control |
| Supabase CLI | Latest | For local dev and migrations |
| Supabase Account | — | Free tier works for development |

### 11.2 Environment Variables

**Frontend** ([neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/.env](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/.env)):

```env
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
```

**Backend Express** ([neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/backend/.env](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/backend/.env)):

```env
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
```

### 11.3 Local Development Setup

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone <repo-url>
cd neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids

# 2. Install dependencies
bun install

# 3. Copy and configure environment variables
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your Supabase credentials

# 4. Apply database migrations
supabase db push

# 5. Deploy the edge function (adaptive AI)
supabase functions deploy adaptive-ai-helper

# 6. Start the development server
npm run dev
# App runs at: http://localhost:5173
```

### 11.4 Building for Production

```bash
# Build optimised bundle
npm run build

# Preview the production bundle locally
npm run preview

# Deploy to Vercel (recommended)
vercel deploy --prod

# OR deploy to Netlify
netlify deploy --prod --dir=dist
```

### 11.5 Supabase Database Migrations

Migrations are stored in `supabase/migrations/` and applied in timestamp order:

| Migration | Date | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `20251211...` | Dec 2025 | Initial schema: profiles, user_roles, child_profiles, parental_settings |
| `20251222...` | Dec 2025 | Add game_sessions table |
| `20260122...` | Jan 2026 | Add child_behavior_profiles (AI engine) |
| `20260211...` | Feb 2026 | Fix age constraint (1–25) |
| `20260214...` | Feb 2026 | Add remote_control_settings + realtime |

To apply all migrations to a new Supabase project:

```bash
supabase db push
```

### 11.6 Supabase Edge Function Deployment

The `adaptive-ai-helper` function lives in `supabase/functions/adaptive-ai-helper/`. It runs on Deno and receives POST requests with a JSON body containing `{action, childId, gameData, behaviorProfile, currentQuestion}`.

```bash
# Deploy function
supabase functions deploy adaptive-ai-helper

# Test locally
supabase functions serve adaptive-ai-helper
```

### 11.7 Key Configuration Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [vite.config.ts](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/vite.config.ts) | Vite build config, path aliases (`@/`) |
| [tailwind.config.ts](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/tailwind.config.ts) | Custom color tokens (duo-green, duo-purple, pastel-lavender…) |
| [tsconfig.app.json](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/tsconfig.app.json) | TypeScript compiler options for the app |
| [components.json](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/components.json) | Shadcn/UI configuration |
| [supabase/config.toml](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/supabase/config.toml) | Supabase project local config |
| [.env](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/.env) | Environment secrets (never commit this file) |

### 11.8 Custom Design Tokens

All brand colors are defined in [tailwind.config.ts](file:///p:/Project%20nuero/nk5/neuro-frontend/neuronest-kids/tailwind.config.ts):

| Token | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `duo-green` | #58CC02 | Correct answer, success |
| `duo-red` | #FF4B4B | Wrong answer, error |
| `duo-blue` | #1CB0F6 | Interactive elements |
| `duo-purple` | #8549BA | Primary brand, AI indicator |
| `duo-yellow` | #FFD900 | Stars, score |
| `duo-orange` | #FF9600 | Warnings, struggling state |
| `duo-teal` | #00CD9C | Secondary accents |
| `pastel-lavender` | — | Game background gradient top |
| `pastel-mint` | — | Game background gradient bottom |

